# s29b_security_part3.oot — (Part 3 of s29b_security.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/s29b_security.oot`.

## emit-bc (HIGH residual — not the Z2 class)
`bc_emit*` still does **not** call `check_secret_println_sinks`. Live:

| Probe | emit-bc | Bytes |
|-------|---------|-------|
| 01 `println(tok)` | **rc=0** | `PUSH_STR s3cret` / `CALL println 1` |
| 06 `println((n), tok)` | **rc=0** | `LOAD_LOCAL 0` / `LOAD_LOCAL 1` / `CALL println 2` |
| p+ grouping+concat | **rc=0** | `PUSH_STR s` / `PUSH_STR x` / `CALL println 1` |

SECRET **reaches** the BC `println` opcode. Orthogonal to 2.9 unify.
Do **not** soft-pass.

---

## Root-cause (why Z1/Z3 hold and Z2/Z5 do not)
1. **Z1** — simple arg lists have no inner `RPAREN` before the SECRET
   IDENT. Front-door + stmt belt + (llvm) front-door all see it.
2. **Z2 F1** — shipping front-door is a **flat** RPAREN stop. LLVM and
   wasm have **no second rail**. Stmt `c_emit_println` **does**
   continue after `c_emit_expr_c`, so emit-c still BLOCK on later-arg.
   That is why later-arg emit-c refuse does not save Z2.
3. **Z2 F3/F4** — SECRET sits in the **same** arg after an inner
   `RPAREN`. Stmt IDENT scan stops; `c_emit_expr_c` lowers the rest
   and prints it. eprintln is saved only by rail (3).
4. **Z3** — STRING is not IDENT. Walker never treats string text as a
   name.
5. **Unify is not landed.** `c_emit_ident_stmt` still early-returns
   to `c_emit_println`. L175–193 (ELF) / L173–200 (WT) is still a
   token loop, not `c_secret_emit_guard(env, id, …)`.

