## Residual risks (return)
| ID | Sev | Residual | Why not extra 2.9 FAIL |
|----|-----|----------|------------------------|
| R1 | **HIGH** | Check/LLVM/wasm later-arg after inner `RPAREN` (F1/F2) | **This is the 2.9 FAIL** |
| R1b | **HIGH** | Stmt println grouping+concat / nest **prints** SECRET (F3) | Same hole class; emit-c leak |
| R2 | HIGH | `emit-bc` skips the walker; `CALL println` gets SECRET | Backend wiring; walker never runs |
| R3 | MED | Stmt `println` ≠ `c_secret_emit_guard` (unify still OPEN) | Engineering of 2.9 |
| R4 | MED | LLVM builtin `print` / first-arg-only (s71 R2) | `print` not a typed product API |
| R5 | MED | 2.10 user wrapper `leak(tok)` → `oo_print_str(x)` | Separate sprint |
| R6 | MED | 5.8 `${}` interp not implemented | Literal string |
| R7 | LOW | Walker LPAREN-optional scan-forward | Accidental refuse / FP class, not a hide |
| R8 | MED | `let f = println; f((n), tok)` emit-c/llvm tcache abort | Host emit residual; check FN; not a print |
| R9 | — | Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interproc beyond `__fr_secret__` | `SECRET_TAINT.oot` |
| R10 | — | 2.8 macro second pass | **Closed residual-doc**; do not reopen |
| R11 | — | WT `depth` unshipped | Named so peers do not ACCEPT source-only |

**Explicitly not residuals of this close:** T1 return/alias/if (fixtures
green); T2 string-FP (green); 6.1 `env_set` (other OWN).

